e type of the given place
            entity including natural environment and landscape. In LIDO
            v1.1 these values can be expressed in greater detail through
            &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#placeClassification">lido:placeClassification</a>&gt;.
            Note that Place Classification in LIDO corresponds to ‘<a
            href="https://www.getty.edu/research/tools/vocabularies/guidelines/tgn_3_6_place_types.html">Place
            Type</a>’ in the <a
            href="https://www.getty.edu/research/tools/vocabularies/tgn/index.html">Getty
            Thesaurus of Geographic Names</a>. It is recommended to use
            a URI to refer to the kind of geographical entity.</p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong> For an analogous example see
            ‘lido:politicalEntity’ below in this list.</p>
            <blockquote>
            <p>For more information see the note for ‘<a
            href="http://lido-schema.org/documents/terminology-recommendation.html#geographicalEntity">geographicalEntity</a>’
            in the LIDO Terminology Recommendation.</p>
            </blockquote>
            <h3 data-number="5.4.7" id="label"><span
            class="header-section-number">5.4.7</span> <span
            class="citation" data-cites="label">@label</span></h3>
            <p><strong>Attribute name:</strong> <a
            href="http://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#label">lido:label</a></p>
            <p><strong>Note:</strong> Attribute for many LIDO elements
            to indicate how the data element from which the data were
            migrated is labelled at the user interface. Note that this
            can be different from how the element is named in the source
            database (see <a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#encodinganalog"><em>lido:encodinganalog</em></a>
            for this case).</p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong> The following XML code snippet
            marks the label for the “Historique” note displayed at the
            user interface of the <a
            href="https://www.pop.culture.gouv.fr/notice/joconde/000PE025604">PORTRAIT
            DE MONA LISA (1479-1528)</a>.</p>
            <div class="sourceCode" id="cb51"><pre
            class="sourceCode xml"><code class="sourceCode xml"><span id="cb51-1"><a href="#cb51-1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>&lt;<span class="kw">lido:descriptiveNoteValue</span></span>
<span id="cb51-2"><a href="#cb51-2" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">    lido:label=</span><span class="st">&quot;Historique&quot;</span></span>
<span id="cb51-3"><a href="#cb51-3" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">    xml:lang=</span><span class="st">&quot;fr&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb51-4"><a href="#cb51-4" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    Commandé par le florentin Francesco del Giocondo, époux de Mona Lisa entre 1503 et 1506</span>
<span id="cb51-5"><a href="#cb51-5" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>&lt;/<span class="kw">lido:descriptiveNoteValue</span>&gt;</span></code></pre></div>
            <h3 data-number="5.4.8" id="measurementsgroup"><span
            class="header-section-number">5.4.8</span> <span
            class="citation"
            data-cites="measurementsGroup">@measurementsGroup</span></h3>
            <p><strong>Attribute name:</strong> <a
            href="http://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#measurementsGroup">lido:measurementsGroup</a></p>
            <p><strong>Note:</strong> Attribute for &lt;<a
            href="http://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#eventObjectMeasurements">lido:eventObjectMeasurements</a>&gt;
            and &lt;<a
            href="http://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#objectMeasurementsSet">lido:objectMeasurementsSet</a>&gt;
            to indicate the kind of measurements given in multiple
            &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#measurementsSet">lido:measurementsSet</a>&gt;
            elements. This attribute is intended to be used in
            application profiles.</p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong> The following XML code snippet
            shows how the “<a
            href="http://terminology.lido-schema.org/lido00923">Measurement
            object requirement</a>” concerning temperature conditions is
            recorded.</p>
            <div class="sourceCode" id="cb52"><pre
            class="sourceCode xml"><code class="sourceCode xml"><span id="cb52-1"><a href="#cb52-1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="co">&lt;!-- Measurement object requirement for @measurementsGroup &quot;temperature&quot; --&gt;</span></span>
<span id="cb52-2"><a href="#cb52-2" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>&lt;<span class="kw">lido:eventObjectMeasurements</span></span>
<span id="cb52-3"><a href="#cb52-3" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">    lido:type=</span><span class="st">&quot;http://terminology.lido-schema.org/lido00923&quot;</span></span>
<span id="cb52-4"><a href="#cb52-4" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">    lido:measurementsGroup=</span><span class="st">&quot;http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300056066&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb52-5"><a href="#cb52-5" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;<span class="kw">lido:displayObjectMeasurements</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb52-6"><a href="#cb52-6" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        16-25°C ± 1.5°C over 24 hours if the object is installed in a room</span>
<span id="cb52-7"><a href="#cb52-7" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        equipped with an operating Heating Ventilation and Air-Conditioning</span>
<span id="cb52-8"><a href="#cb52-8" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        (HVAC) system</span>
<span id="cb52-9"><a href="#cb52-9" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;/<span class="kw">lido:displayObjectMeasurements</span>&gt;</span></code></pre></div>
            <h3 data-number="5.4.9" id="mostnotableevent"><span
            class="header-section-number">5.4.9</span> <span
            class="citation"
            data-cites="mostNotableEvent">@mostNotableEvent</span></h3>
            <p><strong>Attribute name:</strong> <a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#mostNotableEvent">lido:mostNotableEvent</a></p>
            <p><strong>Note:</strong> Attribute for &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#eventSet">lido:eventSet</a>&gt;
            and &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#eventWrap">lido:eventWrap</a>&gt;
            to indicate that the event in focus is considered to be the
            most notable or significant event among others recorded for
            the object.</p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong> The following XML code snippet
            declares the event “<a
            href="http://terminology.lido-schema.org/lido00007">Production</a>”
            as the most notable one.</p>
            <div class="sourceCode" id="cb53"><pre
            class="sourceCode xml"><code class="sourceCode xml"><span id="cb53-1"><a href="#cb53-1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>&lt;<span class="kw">lido:eventSet</span></span>
<span id="cb53-2"><a href="#cb53-2" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">    lido:sortorder=</span><span class="st">&quot;1&quot;</span></span>
<span id="cb53-3"><a href="#cb53-3" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">    lido:mostNotableEvent=</span><span class="st">&quot;1&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb53-4"><a href="#cb53-4" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;<span class="kw">lido:event</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb53-5"><a href="#cb53-5" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        &lt;<span class="kw">lido:eventType</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb53-6"><a href="#cb53-6" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>            &lt;<span class="kw"